      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to find the remainder when \\(-3737\\) is divided by \\(8\\). This can be done by adding \\(8\\) repeatedly until we get a positive number.\n\nFirst, let's reorganize \\(-3737\\):\n\n\\[\n-3737 = -(422 \\cdot 8) - 3\n\\]\n\nNow, dividing \\(-3737\\) by \\(8\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Quotient} & = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{-3737}{8} \\right\\rfloor = -467.125 \\\\\n\\text{Remainder} & = -3737 - (-1 \\cdot 422 \\cdot 8) = 7\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n-3737 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( n = 7 \\).\n\nLet’s confirm this using Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate remainder\nremainder = -3737 % 8\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe calculations confirm that the integer \\( n \\) that satisfies \\( 0 \\leq n \\leq 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\) is \n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
